  "surprise": "667 (645/689/668) vs 153's 687 (676/700/685): every seed below its 153 counterpart (-31/-11/-17). Pretraining looked as predicted or better: 4,429-4,478 steps (153: 4,540), final val 0.081-0.085 (153: 0.088) with 0.077-0.082 at 285 s, held-out greedy 0.965-0.978 (153: 0.9675), 9,973,776 params, RL sampling 225-279 samples/s (bench's 182 was pessimistic). The loss went where the RL did not: round-1 sample accuracy fell to 0.224/0.236/0.273 (mean 0.244 vs 153's 0.271) and round-1 solved to 666/707/713 (153: 766), so the logit-side trigram shortcut perturbed the T=0.8 sampler exactly as the pre-registered risk said, and although the fine-tune rounds recovered most of it (RL-solved 1,142/1,159/1,143 vs 1,157), the transfer eval did not. 154's +7 with the exact table on the 256-wide bigram incumbent does not transfer to the 384-wide trunk (rank-36 factoring and width are confounded here); bench_pretrain's 60-s sample_acc (0.057 vs 0.013 for the bigram-input variant) did not predict round-1 accuracy. Lead: round-1 Lean parse-fail was 23-34% of 48,000 samples; worth reading 153's driver logs for the same figure before blaming the table.",
